# Example only, shown in Go — your Makefile is yours to write in whatever language
# you choose. These two targets are the contract (BRIEF.md §3.1); everything else is
# optional.

.PHONY: run test
PORT ?= 8080

## run: start everything; the API must be answering on $(PORT) within 180s,
## including any image build this target triggers on a cold machine.
## If you use docker compose, bring it up here — `make run` is the whole interface.
## Your server must implement this flag, or read PORT itself.
run:
	go run ./cmd/server -addr=:$(PORT)

## test: your own tests; no separately running service. Exit nonzero on failure.
## Start/clean up test dependencies here or in test setup; stdout/stderr are the report.
## `-race` below is Go's race detector and is shown only because this example is Go.
## Use whatever your runtime offers, or nothing if it offers nothing.
test:
	go test ./... -race
